{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And He said: If you will diligently heed the voice of HaShem, etc. — all the disease, etc.</b> Just as your eyes saw that it is in My power to heal one bitter thing by means of another bitter thing like it, from now on take upon yourself to heed the voice of HaShem and to do what is right in His eyes — and even though the Torah and the commandments appear at their beginning to be hard and bitter, in the end they are sweet, for they are ״מַרְפֵּא לָעֶצֶם וְרִפְאוּת לְשָׁרֶךָ״ (a healing to the bone and marrow), and they save you from all the disease which I placed upon Egypt — whether illness of bodies or illness of souls on account of the matter of their stiff-neckedness. And if you do not feel the innate property of the Torah, that it should be for you a remedy in this manner — behold, ״אֲנִי ה׳ רֹפְאֶיךָ״, and only the healer needs to know the innate property of the healing substances, but the one being healed does not need to know this; he need only trust in the faithful healer." "Another matter. That He said: Why do I warn you not to come to illness? Because ״אֲנִי ה׳ רֹפְאֶךָ״ — and the way of every healer is to warn those he loves to guard themselves from the things that cause illness, so that they will not need to engage afterward in curing them. Thus do I teach you to benefit from things that preserve health, so that you will not come to illness — because ״אֲנִי ה׳ רֹפְאֶךָ״, guiding you in the way you should go."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:20:45.045508520Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}